- **Domain:** BLUEMOONTUESDAY

**Malware Family:** Remcos RAT (Remote Control and Surveillance)
**Attribution Confidence:** Behavioral (based on traffic patterns and IOC characteristics)

**Incident Summary:**
A Windows workstation (DESKTOP-L8C5GSJ, 10.1.17.215) belonging to user shutchenson was compromised with Remcos RAT. The infection chain involved delivery of obfuscated PowerShell loaders from 5.252.153.241, which downloaded additional payloads including fake TeamViewer executables and secondary scripts. The malware established command-and-control communication to 45.125.66.32:2917 with encrypted channels and beacon calls to 5.252.153.241 reporting execution status. Large data transfers (up to 5.3 MB per connection) suggest information exfiltration or staging of additional tools.

